  "register": "notes",
  "source_dataset": "MIMIC_IV_NOTE",
  "text": "Allergies:\nNaprosyn / Metoprolol / Nsaids / Verapamil / Sulfa \n(Sulfonamides)\n\nChief Complaint:\nFevers\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\n___ yo F w/PMHx sx for UGBI, diastolic CHF, CAD, COPD, hx \nfrequent UTIs who is admitted with nausea, vomiting, and fevers \nto 101. Patient was recently started on ciprofloxacin for a UTI, \nand is completing her five day course today. When she developed \nthe fevers to 101, she took tylenol and presented to the ED. She \nhad associated nausea and vomiting, NBNB. She has chronic \ndiarrhea and constipation. She denies chest pain, SOB. She has \nno sick contacts, no recent travel, no changes in her \nmedications other than the ciprofloxacin she has been taking. \nOtherwise she feels well. She currently feels hungry and \nthirsty. She notes urinary frequency, but states that this is \nher baseline. She denies dysuria or odor to her urine. She also \nnotes myalgias. \n.\nIn the ED, she received ceftriaxone. Her UA was negative. She is \nadmitted to medicine for management. \n.\nROS:\n-Constitutional: []WNL []Weight loss []Fatigue/Malaise [x]Fever \n[x]Chills/Rigors []Nightweats []Anorexia\n-Eyes: [x]WNL []Blurry Vision []Diplopia []Loss of Vision \n[]Photophobia\n-ENT: [x]WNL []Dry Mouth []Oral ulcers []Bleeding gums/nose \n[]Tinnitus []Sinus pain []Sore throat\n-Cardiac: [x]WNL []Chest pain []Palpitations ___ edema \n[]Orthopnea/PND []DOE\n-Respiratory: [x]WNL []SOB []Pleuritic pain []Hemoptysis []Cough\n-Gastrointestinal: []WNL [x]Nausea [x]Vomiting []Abdominal pain \n[]Abdominal Swelling [x]Diarrhea [x]Constipation []Hematemesis \n[]Hematochezia []Melena\n-Heme/Lymph: [x]WNL []Bleeding []Bruising []Lymphadenopathy\n-GU: []WNL [x]Incontinence/Retention []Dysuria []Hematuria \n[]DIscharge []Menorrhagia\n-Skin: [x]WNL []Rash []Pruritus\n-Endocrine: [x]WNL []Change in skin/hair []Loss of energy \n[]Heat/Cold intolerance\n-Musculoskeletal: [ ]WNL [x]Myalgias []Arthralgias []Back pain\n-Neurological: [x] WNL []Numbness of extremities []Weakness of \nextremities []Parasthesias []Dizziness/Lightheaded []Vertigo \n[]Confusion []Headache\n-Psychiatric: [x]WNL []Depression []Suicidal Ideation\n-Allergy/Immunological: [x] WNL []Seasonal Allergies\n\nBrief Hospital Course:\nThis is a ___ yo F with a history of chronic diastolic CHF, CAD, \nCOPD, h/o frequent UTIs, admitted with fever, nausea and \nvomiting.\n\n#Viral gastroenteritis - resolved with supportive care\n\n#Acute on Chronic Diastolic CHF: This patient has severe \ndiastolic heart failure. In order to achieve adequate diuresis, \nshe required 100-150 mg of IV lasix BID, 5 mg of Metolazone, and \n25 mg of spironolactone. 4 liters were removed over a 3 day \nperiod, but this became increasingly ineffective, and her \ncreatinine increased from 1.4 to 1.7. She remains hypoxic \nsecondary to unresolved interstitial pulmonary edema. Her \ntherapy will have to be further titrated with these limitations \nin mind.\n\n#Delirium:  Multifactorial and likely related to narcotics and \nacute incurrent illness, ressolved\n\n#Peripheral Neuropathy: Difficult to control. The family was \nconcerned that the long-acting oxycontin was contributing to her \ndelirium, which is possible, but she was in fact taking more \nthan 20 mg /day of oxycodone. The daughter preferred that we add \nneurotin 300 q AM, and stopped oxycontin\n\n#DM II - stable\n\n.\n\nDischarge Diagnosis:\nPrimary:\nViral gastroenteritis\nAcute on chronic diastolic heart failure\nDelirium\n.\nSecondary:\nchronic obstructive pulmonary disease\nDiabetes Mellitus type II\nCoronary artery disease",
